course: dictionary
lesson: 10525
title: Typing and typos
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Typing means writing by pressing the keys of a computer, phone or typewriter. When you type a story, a message or a search, your fingers do the writing.
explain: Typing is also a skill, and people measure it in words per minute. Use context to work out a new word: «A typo is a typing mistake; a mistake doesn't always mean someone doesn't know the rule.» A typo is a slip of the fingers, not proof that someone doesn't know the spelling.
explain: Touch typing means using all your fingers, starting on the home row (the middle row of letter keys). «Touch typing, with all fingers starting on the home row, is much faster in the long run.» It takes practice, but it pays off.
fact: Typing means writing by pressing keys on a computer, phone or typewriter.
fact: Typing speed is measured in words per minute.
fact: Words = speed × minutes, and minutes = words ÷ speed. For example, 25 words per minute for 4 minutes is 100 words.
fact: «A typo is a typing mistake.»
fact: Touch typing uses all your fingers, starting on the home row.
exercise: «A typo is a typing mistake.» What is a typo? | A kind of computer | *A mistake made while typing | A broken keyboard | A very fast typing speed
exercise: Maya types 30 words every minute. How many words does she type in 5 minutes? | *150 | 35 | 300 | 25
exercise: What is the home row? | The top row of number keys | *The middle row of letter keys | The bottom row, next to the space bar | The keys in the corners
test: What is typing speed usually measured in? | Metres per second | Kilograms per hour | *Words per minute | Litres per minute
test: Ben types for 4 minutes at 20 words per minute. How many words is that? | 24 | 5 | 200 | *80
exam: Lily types 240 words at 40 words per minute. How many minutes does it take? | 9 | *6 | 200 | 280
